compression ratio.

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:12.130
It's significantly higher
in encoding and decoding

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:14.537
speeds compared to arithmetic
like that in the Huffman

00:16:14.537 --> 00:16:14.770
coding.

00:16:14.770 --> 00:16:15.340
Yes.

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:17.578
If you look at these two--

00:16:17.578 --> 00:16:20.068
[INAUDIBLE]

00:16:20.068 --> 00:16:21.185
Yeah, but it is rANS.

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:27.180
rANS is the same compression
as arithmetic in this table

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:31.380
and it's just
faster at decoding.

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:33.720
tANS is slightly
overhead, I guess.

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:35.085
It depends on the use case.

00:16:37.950 --> 00:16:39.400
Talk to us.

